.TH TOMATOPLAY 1 "September 2026" "tomatoplay 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tomatoplay, tp \- browse and watch anime, movies, and TV series from multiple sources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tomatoplay
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIquery\fR]
.br
.B tp
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIquery\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tomatoplay
is a CLI tool to search and stream anime, movies, and TV series from multiple
sources. It provides interactive search via fzf/rofi/dmenu, quality selection,
download support, and a watch history.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -s, --source SOURCE
Specify source: all, anidb, aniwatch, gogoanime, 9anime, animeplanet, anisearch, youtube.
.TP
.B -c, --continue
Continue watching from history.
.TP
.B -T, --trending
Browse what's popular right now, without typing a search.
.TP
.B -L, --lucky-tomato
Pluck a random (playable) show off the vine and start playing it.
.TP
.B -d, --download
Download the video instead of playing it.
.TP
.B -D, --delete
Delete history.
.TP
.B -H, --history
Print the watch history (episode per series).
.TP
.B -q, --quality
Specify the video quality.
.TP
.B -v, --vlc
Use VLC to play the video.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Show the version of the script.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.TP
.B -e, --episode, -r, --range
Specify the number of episodes to watch (e.g. 5, or 1-10).
.TP
.B -a, --audio AUDIO
Choose the audio track for the current episode: \fBsub\fR (subtitled,
Japanese) or \fBdub\fR (English dub). When unset and the series has an
English dub, you will be asked interactively after picking an episode;
selecting another audio (where available) hides the prompt. Use
\fBchange_audio\fR in the playback menu to switch during playback.
.TP
.B --dub
Play the English dubbed version (same as \fB-a dub\fR).
.TP
.B --rofi
Use rofi instead of fzf for the interactive menu.
.TP
.B --dmenu
Use dmenu instead of fzf for the interactive menu.
.TP
.B --no-detach
Don't detach the player (useful for in-terminal playback, mpv only).
.TP
.B --exit-after-play
Exit the player and return the player exit code.
.TP
.B -U, --update
Update the script.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_DEFAULT_SOURCE
Default source (default: all).
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_PLAYER
Default player.
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_QUALITY
Default quality.
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Download directory.
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_MENU
Menu program (fzf, rofi, dmenu).
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_MODE
Default audio track (sub, dub). Acts the same as passing \fB-a\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Search all sources for naruto
.B tp naruto
.TP
Search a specific source
.B tp -s gogoanime "one punch"
.TP
Watch specific episodes
.B tp -e 1-10 "one piece"
.TP
Download episodes
.B tp -d "naruto" -e 1-10
.SH DEPENDENCIES
curl, grep, sed, mpv or vlc, yt-dlp or ffmpeg, fzf.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/tomatoplay/history
Watch history.
